# Per-image Trivy exceptions for the third-party compose images.
#
# `third-party-image-scan.yml` passes ONE of these files to the Trivy action for
# the matching image (`trivyignores`). They are deliberately not global: a CVE
# exception accepted for one upstream image must not silence the same CVE in a
# different image (CTR-P2-007).
#
# Every entry must be present in the current upstream image, be upstream
# blocked (newest release already pinned), and carry an expiry. Do NOT add
# first-party (mct-*) image findings here; those are gated by the build-push
# scans. Re-review on the expiry date and drop each line once the upstream
# image is rebuilt.
#
# Exception list reviewed: 2026-11-03. Next review: 2026-12-01.
# --- prom/node-exporter v1.12.1 (digest-pinned in docker-compose.yml) ---
# Added 2026-11-03: the previous global .trivyignore silently suppressed these
# 15 HIGH findings (14 unique CVEs) in the new fifth image (CTR-P2-007). They
# are real and fixable only by an upstream rebuild: node-exporter v1.12.1 is the
# newest release and is built with Go 1.26.5, while the fixes need Go >= 1.26.6
# (some >= 1.26.10). Scoped here explicitly so a future image is not covered by
# the same blanket exception.
